# Distributed Task Queue with Celery, Redis & Docker

This plan outlines the implementation of a distributed task queue using Celery and Redis to offload heavy YOLO inference and OpenCV motion analysis to background worker nodes, providing non-blocking asynchronous processing and real-time task status polling.

## Proposed Architecture

## Proposed Architecture: Parallel Heavy CV Tasks + Downstream Aggregation

You have made a spot-on architectural observation! Event clustering, Heatmaps, and Groq AI depend directly on the output of YOLO detections and OpenCV motion frames.

Furthermore, **YOLO inference** and **OpenCV motion analysis** are independent of each other! That means we can run them in **parallel** across workers using Celery:

```mermaid
graph TD
    Client[Frontend UI] -->|1. Upload Video| API[FastAPI Server]
    API -->|2. Dispatch Parallel Tasks| Redis[(Redis Broker:6379)]
    API -->|3. Return task_id immediately| Client

    subgraph "Distributed Background Workers (Heavy Compute)"
        Redis -->|Task A| Worker1[Worker Node: YOLO Inference]
        Redis -->|Task B| Worker2[Worker Node: OpenCV Motion]
    end

    Worker1 -->|YOLO Detections| Aggregator[Aggregation & Finalization]
    Worker2 -->|Motion Events| Aggregator

    subgraph "Downstream Fast Steps (<2 sec)"
        Aggregator --> Step1[Event Clustering ~5ms]
        Aggregator --> Step2[Heatmap Generation ~20ms]
        Aggregator --> Step3[Groq AI Summary ~1.5s]
        Aggregator --> Step4[Save Session JSON]
    end

    Aggregator -->|Store Result| Redis
    Client -->|4. Poll Status & Progress| API
    API -->|5. Return Live Progress / Session| Client
```

### Why this design is optimal:
1. **Parallel Speedup:** YOLO and OpenCV Motion execute at the same time on worker processes instead of waiting for each other sequentially.
2. **Resource Isolation:** The heavy GPU/CPU crunching is isolated to worker nodes, so the FastAPI web server remains instant (<100ms response time).
3. **Downstream Pipeline:** As soon as YOLO + Motion complete, the lightweight downstream steps (Event Clustering, Heatmaps, and Groq AI) execute automatically to complete the session.

